SUMMARY:(51) Nemausa hides a mag 10.4 star (just outside the path)
DESCRIPTION:(51) Nemausa hides a magnitude 10.4 star\, seen from Chittoor (
 A.P.).\nThe predicted edge passes 12 km to the S\, so a miss is likely —
  but a chord from near the edge is the most valuable observation of all.\n
 Closest approach 21:26:44 IST\, give or take 1 s. The star is 28° up in t
 he WSW · dark sky.\nIt fades 2.5 magnitudes for up to 6.3 s on the centre
  line\, and the path is 138 km wide\, give or take 17 km.\nFinder chart\, 
 the map and the path as KML: https://occult.alokm.com/asteroids-2026-10#20
 26-10-02-51-nemausa-481280
